Revision history for Perl extension PerCUDA

{{$NEXT}}

    - Rebuild of the 2013 prototype for Perl 5.40+ and CUDA 12+
    - Translate kernels written in Perl to CUDA C++ and compile them with
      NVRTC through CUDA::DriverAPI; cache compiled kernels on disk and
      recompile a broken cache entry
    - Run kernels on the GPU or in the perl interpreter with the same results
      (perl_mode => 'compat'), or faster and slightly different ('fast')
    - Add precision => 'single' | 'double' for both engines
    - Pass scalars by value, coalesce memory access, reuse device buffers and
      the CUDA context, convert arrays in C (CUDA::DriverAPI write_array/read_array)
    - Accept PDL ndarrays for array arguments (copied without conversion on
      the GPU engine); PDL stays optional
    - Add examples (eg/), author tests, perltidy, Perl::Critic, gitleaks,
      pre-commit hooks and GitHub Actions
